
Option 2: The Failproof Breakpoint Method (No Script Required)

If the latest security patch completely isolates the scripting layer from the game's internal routing functions, you can activate it through the game's engine inspector seamlessly:
1. In the top-left menu of Bitburner, click Debug -> Activate (or press F12 / Ctrl+Shift+I) to open the Web DevConsole.
2. Click on the Sources tab at the top.
3. In the left-hand folder tree, navigate to: top -> webpack:// -> src -> ui -> GameRoot.tsx.
4. Look for a line containing a switch statement looking at pages (usually switch (pageWithContext.page) around line 198–204).
5. Click the line number to place a blue breakpoint dot next to it.
6. Go back to the game window and click any button on your left menu sidebar (like City or Travel). The game will pause execution.
7. Look at the right-side DevTools panel under Scope -> Local -> pageWithContext.
8. Double-click the value of page (which might say "City") and change it manually to "Dev" (with quotation marks).
9. Click the blue Play/Resume arrow button at the top of DevTools to unpause.
